<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buenos Aires</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buenos Aires is a port city on the estuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, first founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-mendoza">Pedro de Mendoza</a> in 1536 and refounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-garay">Juan de Garay</a> in 1580. It became the capital of the Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata in 1776 and led the May Revolution of 1810. Rivalry between the city and the other provinces shaped Argentine politics for most of the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buenos-aires.jpg" alt="Buenos Aires" width="320" height="131" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deensel · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puerto_Madero,_Buenos_Aires_(40689219792)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Argentine Republic took its modern form after decades of conflict between <b>Buenos Aires</b> and the interior provinces that followed independence from Spain, declared at the Congress of Tucumán in 1816.</blockquote><a href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentine Republic · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Spain founded Soriano in 1624, Portugal a fort at Colonia del Sacramento in 1680, and Spain Montevideo in 1726 as a stronghold whose harbour soon rivalled <b>Buenos Aires</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/oriental-republic-of-uruguay">Oriental Republic of Uruguay · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Upper Peru had been transferred from the Viceroyalty of Peru to the new Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata in 1776, so both Lima and <b>Buenos Aires</b> claimed it.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia">Republic of Bolivia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>When <b>Buenos Aires</b> set up its own junta in May 1810, a congress in Asunción refused to accept its authority.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-paraguay">Republic of Paraguay · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>On 24 or 25 May 1810 an Open Cabildo in <b>Buenos Aires</b> removed him, and the Primera Junta was formed on 25 May under Cornelio Saavedra, with Mariano Moreno and Juan José Paso as secretaries.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…Viceroyalty of New Granada was carved out of its northern territories in 1717, suppressed in 1723 and permanently restored in 1739, and in 1776 the creation of the Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata took Upper Peru and Potosí, whose silver now flowed out through <b>Buenos Aires</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
